  "launcherHazards": {
    "note": "Confirmed 2026-08-23. Two separate overhead hazards for the Launcher Conveyor, distinct from the landingGapTable (which was measured clear of both). (1) Low ceiling in the original 20x20 zone (x:0-19, y:0-19 — matches knownZoneRects tier 2) caps the safe launch angle per power level; angles above the cap hit the ceiling instead of following the normal arc. (2) In the taller expansion, ceiling-mounted light fixtures run perpendicular to the delivery doors, spanning the full depth at each x position — a package launched parallel to the doors (facing along the x-axis) can clip one. Light x-positions are close estimates, not exact-tile precision (this is a warning-level feature, not a collision calculator, since we don't have a height-vs-distance trajectory profile). Only one clearance data point is confirmed (power 7 needs angle <= 50 to clear); lower power/angle combos are untested but presumed safer since their arcs are lower.",
    "lowCeilingZone": { "x": 0, "y": 0, "w": 20, "h": 20 },
    "ceilingMaxAngle": { "2": 70, "3": 70, "4": 65, "5": 50, "6": 35, "7": 35 },
    "lightPositionsX": [22, 26, 31, 35.5, 41, 45.5],
    "lightClearance": { "power7MaxAngle": 50 }
  }
